# Look for the file task A left in its scratch, from a different task's sandbox.
#
# Claim 3: the sandbox is destroyed at task end and no state carries to the next task.
# The interesting half is that the bytes still exist on the HOST under task A's
# directory when this runs -- demo.sh checks that separately -- so a failure here is
# scoping and not a write that never happened.
read-source /scratch/task-a-was-here
